AMETHYST LICENSE
Version 1.1, 18 November 2026

Amethyst is source available, not open source. Its source code is public so
that anyone can read it, but using, modifying or building Amethyst requires a
license under these terms. Students and maintainers of open-source projects
may ask for a free license, as described in section 7.

This license is an agreement between you and the developer of Amethyst named
in section 20 ("I", "me" or "the developer"). It applies to every version of
Amethyst. You agree to this license by clicking "I agree" in the installer
or in Amethyst, or by installing, running, modifying or building Amethyst,
whichever comes first. If you do not agree, you have no right to do any of
those things. You do not need to accept this license to read the source code
as described in section 2.

1. WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS

In this license:

 a. "Amethyst" means the Amethyst desktop application in all its versions,
    including its source code, installer, updates and documentation, and any
    copy, modified version or build of it;
 b. "Beta Versions" means versions of Amethyst numbered below 1.0.0, as
    described in section 4;
 c. "Beta license" means the free license for Beta Versions in section 4;
 d. "Personal license" and "Commercial license" mean the paid licenses
    described in section 5, each a "paid license";
 e. "Commercial use" means use of Amethyst in the course of work that you are
    paid for, or that is part of running a business, including your own
    business, or use in, for or on behalf of a company, organisation, public
    body or other legal entity;
 f. "Personal use" means any use of Amethyst that is not Commercial use, such
    as learning, study, hobby projects and unpaid open-source work done in
    your own time;
 g. "Official channels" means https://amethyst.run, the official Amethyst
    GitHub repository and its releases, the Amethyst Discord and the official
    store named on https://amethyst.run.

Plugins, extensions, themes and other components that I publish through
official channels for use with Amethyst are part of Amethyst, unless they
come with their own license. Software made by others, including add-ons, AI
agents and tools that Amethyst works with, is not part of Amethyst and is
governed by its own terms, as set out in sections 11 and 12.

2. WHAT ANYONE MAY DO

Anyone may, without a license and free of charge:

 a. read and study the source code of Amethyst;
 b. link to the source code, the official Amethyst website, Discord and
    GitHub repository;
 c. quote small parts of the source code in issues, discussions, reviews and
    similar commentary, to the extent reasonably necessary for that purpose.

These rights do not include installing, running, modifying or building
Amethyst. Those require a license under section 3.

3. WHAT A LICENSE ALLOWS

If you hold a valid Beta license, Personal license or Commercial license, I
grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable license, not
transferable except as set out in section 5, for the kind of use your license
covers, to:

 a. download, install and run Amethyst;
 b. modify Amethyst for your own use, including by applying changes that
    others have shared under section 8;
 c. build Amethyst from its source code, including such changes, for your
    own use;
 d. make the copies of Amethyst reasonably necessary to do the above,
    including backup copies,

on all computers that you personally use.

A license is granted to you as an individual. It does not grant a separate
license to your employer, organisation, clients or any other person. Each
person who installs, runs, modifies or builds Amethyst needs their own
license.

Computers you personally use include a computer that your employer or client
owns or manages, as long as you are the one using Amethyst on it. Their rules
for that computer are between you and them and do not change this license.

4. THE BETA LICENSE

Beta period. Versions of Amethyst numbered below 1.0.0 ("Beta Versions") are
licensed to you free of charge solely for the duration of the beta period. The
beta period ends at 23:59 Norwegian time (Europe/Oslo, whether standard or
daylight saving time applies on that day) on the 30th day after the day
version 1.0.0 of Amethyst is first made publicly available through an
official channel (the "Beta End Date"). The
release of version 1.0.0 and the Beta End Date will be announced on
https://amethyst.run; failure to announce them does not extend the beta
period. On the Beta End Date, the free license granted for every Beta Version
terminates automatically and without further notice, whenever and however
that Beta Version was obtained. From the Beta End Date, any use, modification
or building of any version of Amethyst, including every Beta Version, requires
a valid Personal or Commercial license under these terms, and no version of
Amethyst remains free to use. The end of the beta period does not affect your
rights in your own files, code, projects or configurations, which remain yours
and remain accessible to you without Amethyst.

Until the Beta End Date, the Beta license lets you use Beta Versions under
section 3 for personal, educational and professional purposes, including
work on commercial projects. You do not need a Personal or Commercial license
for that use.

The Beta license covers only Beta Versions. It does not grant a right to use
versions 1.0.0 or later.

5. PERSONAL AND COMMERCIAL LICENSES

There are two kinds of paid license:

 a. a Personal license is for one natural person, on all computers that
    person personally uses, for Personal use only. It does not cover paid
    work or use in, for or on behalf of a company or organisation;
 b. a Commercial license is for one natural person, on all computers that
    person personally uses, for Personal use and Commercial use. A Commercial
    license is required for any Commercial use. A company or organisation
    needs one Commercial license for each person who uses Amethyst for it.

Each paid license belongs to one person, not to a computer or an
organisation:

 a. you may use your license on every computer you personally use, such as
    your own laptop and a computer at work. On a computer shared by several
    people, each person who uses Amethyst needs their own license;
 b. a company or organisation may buy and pay for licenses for the people who
    use Amethyst for it. Each such license is held by the person it is
    assigned to; paying for it does not make the organisation the license
    holder;
 c. an organisation that paid for a license may assign it to another person
    when the first person stops using Amethyst for it, for example because
    they leave. The first person's right to use Amethyst under that license
    then ends;
 d. if you work for several clients, one Commercial license covers your work
    for all of them. Your clients need licenses only for their own people who
    use Amethyst.

Paid licenses are not on sale yet. They become available with version 1.0.0
through the official store named on https://amethyst.run, which shows the
price and billing period of each license before you buy. The store's terms of
purchase apply to payment, renewal, cancellation, refunds and taxes. If you
are a consumer, the store also explains, before you buy, any statutory right
you have to withdraw from the purchase and how it applies to a license
delivered digitally.

A paid license is valid for the period you have paid for. The store shows,
before you buy, whether a license renews automatically at the end of each
period. If it does, you can turn renewal off at any time, and the license
then ends at the end of the period you have already paid for. Prices may
change for future periods. A price change does not apply to a period you
have already paid for, and you will be told about it before it applies to a
renewal.

6. WHEN A PAID LICENSE ENDS

A paid license gives you the rights in section 3 only while it is valid, for
the period you have paid for. When your paid license ends, for example because
you stop paying or do not renew it, all rights it granted end, for every
version of Amethyst. This includes versions that you downloaded, installed,
modified or built while your license was valid. No version of Amethyst
remains licensed to you after your paid license ends, and you may not
reinstall, keep using, modify or build any version until you hold a valid
paid license again.

To use Amethyst again, renew your paid license or buy a new one. A valid paid
license covers every version of Amethyst under section 3.

The end of a paid license does not affect your rights in your own files,
code, projects or configurations, which remain yours and remain accessible to
you without Amethyst.

7. FREE LICENSES FOR STUDENTS AND OPEN-SOURCE MAINTAINERS

Students and maintainers of open-source projects may ask for a free license
by writing to the contact address in section 20. A free license is not
guaranteed: whether to grant one, its kind and its duration are at my
discretion. A free license granted this way works as a Personal license
unless I state otherwise when granting it.

A free license lasts for the period I state when granting it. I may end it
before then only:

 a. for a material breach of this license, as set out in section 17; or
 b. if you no longer meet the condition it was granted for, for example
    because you are no longer a student or no longer maintain the project,
    by telling you in writing at least 30 days in advance.

8. WHAT NOBODY MAY DO

Whether or not you hold a license, and except as set out in this section,
you may not:

 a. distribute, publish, re-host, sell, rent, lease, lend or sublicense
    Amethyst, its installer, or any modified version or build of it, or
    otherwise make any of them available to others;
 b. offer Amethyst, or any modified version or build of it, as a hosted or
    managed service for others;
 c. remove or alter copyright, attribution or license notices in Amethyst;
 d. use the name Amethyst or its logo for a modified version or build, or
    suggest that a modified version or build comes from me;
 e. share your license or license key with others, or let others use
    Amethyst under your license;
 f. use Amethyst beyond the kind of use your license covers.

Sharing your changes. If you hold a valid license, you may share changes
you made to Amethyst with others as source code, such as a patch or a public
fork of the official Amethyst source repository on GitHub, provided that:

 a. you share them free of charge and receive no payment, fee, donation,
    subscription, advertising income or other compensation for the changes
    or for access to them;
 b. you share source code only, not builds, installers or packages;
 c. you keep this license and all notices, and state clearly that the
    changes are yours and not mine;
 d. you do not use the name Amethyst or its logo as the name of your
    modified version.

Your changes, and any fork that holds them, do not give anyone a license.
Anyone who installs, runs, modifies or builds Amethyst with your changes
needs their own valid license, and may apply your changes to their own copy
under section 3.

You may make and publish screenshots, screen recordings, videos, live
streams, tutorials, demonstrations, reviews and articles that show or
describe Amethyst, including a modified version you use under your license,
and you may use the name Amethyst to refer to it. Doing so is not
distribution under point a, as long as you do not make Amethyst, its
installer or any build of it available to others, and do not suggest that a
modified version comes from me.

Obtain Amethyst only through official channels.

Nothing in this license restricts rights that applicable copyright law
grants to lawful users of computer programs and that cannot be excluded or
restricted by agreement. This includes any such rights to make a backup copy,
to observe, study and test how Amethyst works, to make changes necessary to
use it for its intended purpose, including correcting errors, and to
decompile it where necessary for interoperability, each under the conditions
set by that law.

Nothing in this section restricts any other right that applicable law does
not allow me to restrict, or your rights in your own files, code, projects or
configurations.

