17. ENDING THE LICENSE

You may end your license at any time by uninstalling Amethyst and ceasing
all use of it. Ending a paid license early does not by itself entitle you to
a refund; the store's terms of purchase apply. This does not affect any
statutory right of withdrawal you have as a consumer.

If you materially breach this license, I may end your license by telling
you in writing. Before I do, I will tell you in writing what the breach is
and give you at least 14 days to remedy it, unless the breach cannot be
remedied or was deliberate, such as distributing builds of Amethyst or
sharing a license key. If you remedy the breach in time, your license
continues.

The Beta license ends on the Beta End Date as set out in section 4.

I may stop distributing Amethyst, or stop providing updates or support, at
any time. Doing so does not, by itself, terminate the rights you have already
received, except that the Beta license still ends on the Beta End Date.

If your license is terminated or ends, you must stop using every version of
Amethyst and delete copies of it in your possession, except where retention
is required or permitted by applicable law. This does not apply to your own
files, code, projects or configurations.

Sections concerning ownership, third-party software, feedback, warranty
disclaimers, liability, governing law and any provisions that by their
nature should survive will continue to apply after termination.

